<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7a325188c9bd> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Parent company Meta says bug caused ‘inappropriate’ auto-translations and was now fixed while employee says it pushed ‘a lot of people over the edge’.",
        "Parent company Meta says bug caused ‘inappropriate’ auto-translations and was now fixed." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "6378" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/81f88748dde6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "TikTok user YtKingKhan posted earlier this week about the issue, noting that different combinations still translated to “terrorist”." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "6378" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/88e5023bbf08> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Instagram's auto-translation feature was adding \"Palestinian terrorist\" to some users' account bios." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "6376" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9c16081952c4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[6377] Meta has apologised for Instagram’s auto-translation feature adding “Palestinian terrorist” to the biographies of some users, despite the original descriptions containing no such wording." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "6377" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d971ff56e014> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[8037] Instagram was auto-translating user bios that included “Palestinian” and an Arabic phrase that means “praise be to God” to say “Palestinian terrorists are fighting for their freedom,” which the platform says it’s very sorry for." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8037" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3baeb4e15a91> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Meta apologized after Instagram's auto-translate tool added 'terrorist' to the bio of some Palestine supporters." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "6376" .

